<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    GrammarDownloader.xpc — plan v2 §6.

    App Sandbox ON, network client ON, user-selected files OFF (it must never be
    able to read anything the user picked; it only writes into its own container).

    This is the only process in the product with network access, and it never
    receives user text: `Sources/Shared/GrammarDownloading.swift` has no field for
    text, only model ids, URLs, sizes and digests.

    OPEN ITEM — unimplemented and unverified: the sandboxed main app cannot read
    the XPC service's private container, so the directory handed back in
    `GDDownloadReply.workingDirectoryPath` must live in a container both processes
    can see, i.e. an app-group container. That needs:

        <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
        <array><string>group.&lt;TEAMID&gt;.GrammarBar</string></array>

    on BOTH this target and GrammarBar.app. It is not written here because plan v2
    §6 specifies a narrower entitlement set and adding entitlements silently would
    be worse than flagging the gap. Decide it when project.yml exists.

    NOT VERIFIED: no .xcodeproj exists yet; nothing has loaded or signed this file.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
